body:
Investigation notes:

- This was working in 0.73.1; it's broken in 0.74.0 +
- The issue is inside a utility function in react-color's `Saturation.js` code:
```js
function getContainerRenderWindow() {
    var container = this.container;

    var renderWindow = window;
    while (!renderWindow.document.contains(container) && renderWindow.parent !== renderWindow) {
        renderWindow = renderWindow.parent;
    }
    return renderWindow;
}
```

Looks like it's reaching up into the parent iframe.

- We did *not* update `react-color` in the 0.73.0..0.74.0 diff
- But `react`, `react-dom`, etc, did get updated
- `react-color` repo: https://github.com/casesandberg/react-color
- I think [this is the problem line](https://github.com/casesandberg/react-color/blob/bc9a0e1dc5d11b06c511a8e02a95bd85c7129f4b/src/components/common/Saturation.js#L23)
- Oh, someone's already opened a bug! https://github.com/casesandberg/react-color/issues/806. But the bug is 4 months old w/o a response, and the project seems unmaintained.
